<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine pension funds yield 21.45 pct.</title>
<headline>Argentine pension funds yield 21.45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's private pension funds achieved an average return of 21.45 percent on their investments in the year to October, the Superintendencia de AFJPs, the body that monitors the funds, said Friday.</p>
<p>In the year to September, the funds achieved an average return of 20.42 percent.</p>
<p>The maximum return attained in the year to October was 27.89 percent while the lowest was 15.02 percent, said the Superintendencia.</p>
<p>The average annual return since the private pension funds were first established in the middle of 1994 was 16.95 percent.</p>
<p>-- Walter Bianchi, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0633</p>
</text>
